  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[airbnb-for-meeting-rooms]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <title>
      <Value><![CDATA[Airbnb for Meeting Rooms]]></Value>
    </title>
    <tagline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Stay in Aquarium 2. Whiteboard and cold coffee included.]]></Value>
    </tagline>
    <demoFeatures>
      <Value><![CDATA[Instant Book
HDMI Roulette
Whiteboard View
Late Checkout]]></Value>
    </demoFeatures>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[Monetise every meeting room | Rent out the room with no windows by the night. We call that 'blackout curtains'.
Glass walls, private meetings | Frosted film on every glass room so the office stops reading your slides. 400 rooms, one roll of film.
End double bookings forever | The dream. Estimated at 13 points in 2019. Still in progress.
Meeting room experiences | Guests join a real status meeting. 'Authentic, long, and nobody knew why I was there.'
Global room inventory | Every room named after a city, a fjord or a Star Wars planet, in one search box.
Sleep in the office, legally | HR, Legal and Facility need to agree. They cannot find a room to meet in.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Whiteboard view | As a guest, I want a whiteboard view so that I wake up to 'DO NOT ERASE' from 2022.
Evict the squatters | As a booker, I want my room at 10:00 so that the people who 'just need 5 more minutes' leave.
A cable that fits | As a guest, I want one cable that fits my laptop so that I do not have to present from my phone.
Check-in by hovering | As a host, I want guests to check in by standing outside the glass so that it gets awkward fast.
Honest reviews | As a guest, I want to write '2 stars, smelled of tuna lunch' so that others are warned.
Find the room | As a new hire, I want directions to 'Valhalla' so that I stop walking into the kitchen.
Ghost meeting cleanup | As a host, I want to cancel the weekly meeting of someone who left in 2020 so that Friday is free.
Monday surge | As a host, I want surge pricing at 09:00 on Mondays so that the weekly kickoff finally costs something.
Cancel without guilt | As a booker, I want to release the room so that... no. I will keep it. Just in case.
Minibar | As a PM, I want a minibar of sticky notes and dead markers so that it feels like home.
The big one, for two | As a client, I want the boardroom for two people so that we can sit very far apart.
Long stay in the phone booth | As an introvert, I want to book the phone booth for a week so that I can live there quietly.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[Instant Book | Book the room right now. Someone is already in it. They also used Instant Book.
HDMI Roulette | Six adapters in a basket. One works. It is never the first one you try.
Late Checkout | The meeting before yours runs over by 12 minutes. Always exactly 12.
Amenities list | 'Screen (broken), 7 chairs (5 matching), plant (plastic), mystery remote.'
Climate control | Two settings: sauna or Greenland. Controlled by a panel nobody understands.
Cleaning fee | Charged if you leave cups behind. Everyone leaves cups behind.
Superhost badge | Awarded to hosts who replace the dead markers. Nobody has ever earned it.
Guest capacity | Fits 8. Booked for 14. 'We can just stand.'
Rename your listing | Turn 'Meeting Room 3' into 'The Innovation Hub'. Same room.
Wishlist | Save the one room with a window. You will never get it.
House rules | 'No tuna. No speakerphone. Wipe the board. Yes, that means you.'
Screen sharing | Works on the second attempt. The first attempt shares your private chat.
Characterful seating | That is how we list the squeaky chair.
Self check-in | The tablet by the door says 'Available'. There are nine people inside.
Cake radar | Shows rooms with leftover cake from the last meeting. Our most used feature.
Neighbourhood guide | 'Quiet area, 10 seconds from the printer, loud sales team to the east.']]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[Room booked until 2087 | A recurring 'Weekly sync' with no end date. The organiser left in 2019. Cannot be deleted.
Two meetings, one room | The system says both teams have it. Both are right. It is now one awkward meeting.
Screen shows last guest's desktop | We all saw the open tab with the job listings. Nobody said a word.
Room does not exist | 'Narnia' is in the calendar but not in the building. Three people are still looking.
Lights go out if you sit still | The motion sensor ends the meeting every 8 minutes. The team now waves during retro.
Review posted mid-meeting | '1 star, still here, send help.' It was visible on the big screen.
Door locks from the outside | The 14:00 standup is still in 'Aquarium'. They have ordered pizza.
Whiteboard will not erase | Someone used a permanent marker in 2021. That org chart is now part of the building.]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[The booking system is Outlook | Under the hood: one shared calendar and one colleague who knows which room is which.
Rooms renamed four times | 'Room B' is 'Hawaii' is 'Focus 2' is 'the one by the printer'. All four are in the code.
Door tablet runs Android 4 | It shows the time in Lisbon. We have all learned to do the maths.
The key is under the plant | Our authentication layer is a plastic fern. Security review: pending.
meetingroom_old_DONT_USE | That is the table we use. The one called meetingroom is empty.
The cables behind the TV | A heritage site. Nobody touches it. One of them might be load-bearing.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[CEO Request: I need a room now | 'The big one, with the view.' It was booked by 11 people. Was.
CEO Request: Rent out the canteen | 'Weddings? Birthdays?' The canteen has not been asked. The canteen will have opinions.
CEO Request: Name a room after me | 'Nothing big,' says the CEO, pointing at the big one.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Book Meeting Room 3. Someone's already in it.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[Rent a meeting room by the hour, the night or the quarter. Whiteboard with last year's strategy included. HDMI cable not guaranteed.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Book a room]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Authentic local experience | Every room comes with a real person saying 'we did actually book this' at two minutes past.
Superhost: Reception | Rated 4.9 stars. Knows where the adapter is. Will not tell you until you have checked in.
All amenities, sort of | Screen, speaker and 14 cables. None fit your laptop. The coffee flask is from the previous booking.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[Lovely stay. Someone knocked at 10:00 sharp and stared through the glass. Just like home.
The room was called 'Innovation'. It had no windows. Five stars.
We booked it for a quick sync. We have lived here since Tuesday.
Cleaning fee: wipe the whiteboard. Nobody dared. It said DO NOT ERASE, dated 2022.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[Free if you just walk in and look confident. Cleaning fee: carry your own cups out.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© Airbnb for Meeting Rooms. Check-out is five minutes before the hour. Nobody has ever complied.]]></Value>
    </siteFooterLine>
